Experimental Compositor Kit
===========================

Overview
--------
The Experimental Compositor Kit provides a lightweight client API for talking to
an experimental compositor service. The API is intentionally small and is meant
for prototyping new effects outside of the primary Interface Kit.

Public API
----------
The public entry point is the BExperimentalCompositor class. The class exposes
methods to connect, set an effect name, and upload a raw texture payload. The
API is declared in <ExperimentalCompositorKit.h>.

Protocol
--------
Messages are exchanged using the service name
"x-vnd.haiku-experimental-compositor" and the message codes defined in
<experimentalcompositor/ExperimentalCompositorProtocol.h>. The current protocol
version is B_EXPERIMENTAL_COMPOSITOR_PROTOCOL_VERSION and clients should send
and expect replies with the kExperimentalCompositorLastError status field.

Sample
------
The ExperimentalCompositor app under src/apps/experimentalcompositor demonstrates
connecting to the service, setting an effect, uploading a 2x2 texture, and then
exiting. It can be used as a reference for integrating the kit in other code.
